-## Queue and Tickets
+## Queue and Tickets (Implemented)
+
+### Queue
+
+A queue belongs to one entity with:
+- `name`: display name
+- `slug`: unique within the entity
+- `is_active`: flag (default true)
+- `labels_i18n`: optional JSON for localized labels
+
+Queues are managed through `App\Models\Queue` and `App\Actions\CreateQueue` (future).
 
 ### Ticket
 
-Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `called_at` and `called_by` (filled when called). Attributes:
+Unit of service in the queue (implemented in `App\Models\Ticket`). It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `status`, `called_at` and `called_by_user_id` (filled when called). Attributes:
 
+- Display `code`: per-queue sequence `A001`, `A002`, ... (see Display Code below)
 - Source queue — the ticket belongs to **one** queue (within the entity); does not record which totem it came from.
 - Priority (numeric, see below).
 - Issuance timestamp (ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
-- Issuance channel: totem, virtual, printed copy, etc.
+- Issuance channel: totem, virtual, printed copy, etc. (enum: `TicketChannel`)
+- Status: waiting, called (enum: `TicketStatus`)
+- Call fields: `called_at` and `called_by_user_id` (nullable, set when ticket is called)
+
+#### Display Code
+
+Per-queue numeric sequence: `A001`, `A002`, ... up to `A999`, then `A1000`, `A1001`, etc. The code is:
+- Unique within the queue (enforced by DB unique constraint)
+- Generated by insertion order (not string order), so `A999` then `A1000` yields `A1001`
+- Never reused after deletion (A001..A003 with A002 deleted yields A004 next)
+- Malformed legacy codes are skipped: with only `A-X` present, next is `A001`; with `A001` then `A-X`, next is `A002`
+
+Generated via `Ticket::nextCode(int $queueId): string`.
+
+#### Issuance
+
+Ticket issuance is handled by `App\Actions\IssueTicket` (invokable action):
+- Rejects inactive queues (checked inside transaction with row lock)
+- Allocates the next display code
+- Creates ticket as `waiting`, `issued_at = now()`, default channel `virtual`, default priority 0
+- Rejects negative priority with `InvalidArgumentException`
+- Retries up to 10 times on unique code collision (concurrent issuance)
+- Persists nothing on rejection (atomic transaction)
+
+Throws `App\Exceptions\InactiveQueueException` if queue is inactive.
+
+#### Call
+
+Only members of the entity can call (enforced by policy). Calling a ticket:
+- Marks it `called`
+- Records `called_at` (current timestamp) and `called_by_user_id`
+- Can only be done once (throws `LogicException` if already called)
+
+Via `Ticket::call(User $user): void`.
 
 ### Priority
 
